s written in **integer cents**, no decimal point at all (e.g. `25440` = $254.40, `-8825` = a $88.25 refund). This one *must* be converted — `system_b.to_major_units()` already exists to divide by 100 and quantize to `Decimal(\"0.01\")`. Skip this and you're off by a factor of 100, which the module's own docstring says has bitten two prior importers.\n- **C (Calder):** `gross_amount` is plain decimal dollars, 2 places, same shape as A. No conversion needed.\n\nSo only Borough needs a units conversion; Ardent and Calder are already dollars.\n\n**Dates**\n- **A (Ardent):** `posted_on` is already ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`. No conversion needed.\n- **B (Borough):** `value_date` is already ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`. No conversion needed.\n- **C (Calder):** `txn_date` is written **day-first**, `dd/mm/yyyy` (e.g. `02/01/2026` is January 2nd, not February 1st). This must be parsed with day first — get it backwards and rows past the 12th of a month raise on parse while rows on/before the 12th silently land in the wrong month, which is the trap called out in that reader's own comment.\n\nPer `docs/CONVENTIONS.md`, both conversions belong in the reader path (i.e., wherever raw A/B/C row dicts get turned into `Record` objects), so that by the time a `Record` exists, `amount` is always dollars as `Decimal` and `date` is always a real `datetime.date` — the three systems are only comparable after that conversion, never before.", "ttft_ms": 2275, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 9259, "uuid": "f31b24c6-7c7b-467b-a856-b4e9de108334", "ttft_stream_ms": 1612, "time_to_request_ms": 127, "first_content_frame_ms": 2132, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 10.7, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "sonnet", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-ef