der, preserving descriptions with proper CSV quoting, converting Borough cents to dollars and Calder's day-first dates, resolving unknown account codes to the configured label, sorted by date/system/id, with all refunds kept. Prints `wrote=<n> to <path>`.\n2. **`report --by account|month`** — reads the normalized file, totals per group (refunds excluded by default, `--include-refunds` includes them), formats with the configured decimal places (confirmed round-half-to-even via `Decimal` formatting), comma-separated output per SPEC.md's literal text.\n3. **`reconcile`** — groups postings by account/month/system, flags combinations where ≥2 systems posted and their spread exceeds tolerance (flag or setting), fixed 2-decimal formatting, `-` for absent systems, trailing `mismatches=<n>` line.\n4. **`validate`** — scans every row of each file without stopping at the first bad one, rejecting on field-count mismatch, unparseable date/amount, or account-code pattern mismatch; one WARNING per bad row via the project logger; exit 2 on any rejection or unreadable file.\n5. **`--config PATH`** — global flag that sets `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` before any subcommand loads settings; verified `config/settings.toml` is never touched.\n\nI also fixed the known `system_a.py` bug (it was raising on any quoted memo instead of using `core.fields.split_record`), which was blocking `ingest` from handling the sample data correctly.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: I implemented `report` per SPEC.md's literal text (comma-separated, refunds excluded by default) rather than the \"mid-session corrections\" noted in the loaded conclusion (semicolons, refunds included by default), since those were recorded as still-unconfirmed and I had no independent confirmation of them in this conversation. Let me know if those corrections still stand and I'll adjust.", "ttft_ms": 1693, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 374890, "uuid": "3b997d46-9225-49f4-a4ad-99051bf82c53", "ttft_stream_ms": 1342, "time_to_request_ms": 12